# Photo3 Salinity Traits - Workflow

## Codebase map
- defs.py: Simulation classes, Atmosphere, timestep setup
- photosynthesis.py / hydraulics.py / soil.py: mixin sub-models (C3, storage, salty soils)
- species_traits.py: species parameter sets
- functions.py, dics.py: global functions and constants
- SensitivityAnalysis/: phase-based sensitivity runs
  - sensitivity_analysis.py runs a Phase config; post_processing.py makes figures
  - SensitivityAnalysisPlan.md describes the phases
  - "Phase N - name/" folders hold config.yaml and results/<batch_id>/
    (only each batch's frozen config.yaml is tracked)
- Notebooks: *_vN.ipynb (latest version is active); Archive/ holds legacy code
- output/ is generated and gitignored

## Start of each new chat (keep it light)
1. Run `git status -sb` and note branch and ahead/behind vs origin.
2. Use the codebase map above; open other files only if the task needs them.
3. Never read whole .ipynb files during the scan (embedded outputs are huge).
4. Give a 2-3 line status summary, then suggest cleanup items if any:
   untracked or stray files, generated artifacts (e.g. *_executed.ipynb),
   superseded _vN notebooks or scripts to move to Archive/.
   Ask before changing anything.

## Commits
- When a discrete chunk of work is done, propose a commit and ask before pushing.
- Message: imperative, <=72 chars, clauses joined by semicolons
  (e.g. "Add Phase 2 config; plot storage volumes").
- Only stage files related to the work; never commit output/, batch results
  (other than frozen configs) or executed notebooks.
- At each push, repeat the cleanup suggestion check.
- After pushing, suggest starting a new chat for the next chunk of work.
